questionvariables.text:
/* Shared Question Bank Place Value, Rounding and Standard Form PVRS-06
Procedural task: convert a large whole number to standard form a*10^n with 1 <= a < 10.
Interaction reference: Numbas NUMBAS-10751 "Scientific notation: large numbers to scientific notation"
This STACK implementation is independently authored. No source wording or mathematical content is copied. */
/* Generate a three-significant-digit coefficient.
d1 is non-zero. */
d1: rand_with_prohib(1,9,[]);
d2: rand_with_prohib(0,9,[]);
d3: rand_with_prohib(1,9,[]);
/* Vary the magnitude.
Exponent 4 through 7 gives large whole numbers appropriate for this skill. */
exponent: rand_with_prohib(4,7,[]);
/* Exact coefficient. */
coefficient: d1 + d2/10 + d3/100;
/* Construct the corresponding whole number.
coefficient has two decimal places, so multiply its integer digit form by 10^(exponent-2). */
mantissa_integer: d1*100 + d2*10 + d3;
number: mantissa_integer * 10^(exponent-2);
/* Target misconception:
The learner uses a coefficient ten times too large and compensates by reducing the exponent by one.
The value is numerically equivalent, but it is NOT valid standard form because the coefficient is outside 1 <= a < 10. */
wrong_coefficient: coefficient*10;
wrong_exponent: exponent-1;
/* Display decimal coefficient while keeping exact arithmetic internally. */
coefficient_display: float(coefficient);
